Let $v(x)=\log_2(x)$, then $\log_2\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)=v\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)$, or $(v\circ u)(x)$.

Therefore, the derivative of $\log_2\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)$ can be found using **the chain rule**:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}\log_2\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[v\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)\right]&&\gray{\text{Let }v(x)=\log_2(x)}
\\\\
&=v'\Bigl(u(x)\Bigr)\cdot u'(x)&&\gray{\text{The chain rule}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{\ln(2)u(x)}\cdot u'(x)&&\gray{\dfrac{d}{dx}\log_2(x)=\dfrac{1}{\ln(2)x}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{u'(x)}{\ln(2)u(x)}
\end{align}$
